      en: "Ghibli Museum, Mitaka is a remarkable feature of the geography and culture of Japan. A whimsical museum dedicated to the work of the animation studio Studio Ghibli. It showcases the art and technique of animation and houses a small theater showing exclusive short films. Designed by director Hayao Miyazaki himself. The museum's slogan is 'Let's get lost together'. Tickets must be purchased in advance and are highly sought after. This protected area is part of Japan's rich wildlife and flora, from the subtropical forests of Kyushu to the snowy regions of Hokkaido. Like many notable places in Japan, it combines regional character with the legacy of the samurai tradition, Shinto and Buddhist heritage, and the modern industrial nation. Thus, this place contributes to the diverse profile of Japan — from Mount Fuji and Tokyo to the volcanic island arc along the Pacific.",
